<!--
  The tethered phone, third draw. The first was a narrow rounded pill - next
  to a percentage, one element from the ROM's battery, it read as a second
  battery. The second was a handset - unmistakably "phone", but a rotary-era
  object on AR glasses, and in a status row a handset means "call in
  progress". This one is the phone the wearer actually owns: a wide flat slab
  (13 of 24 units - the pill's narrowness was half its problem) with the home
  dash for a screen cue. Proportions after Lucide's smartphone, which stays
  legible at 16px.
-->
